      {
        "id": 56613,
        "name": "pwatson1974",
        "username": "pwatson1974",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-29T14:30:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Everything is in play order. And yes, \"would be dealt\" is handled in step 8. Would be dealt only applies to the final damage total and would be in turn order, But that really only applies to Tempest's Shielding Widns interacting with the other 5+ reduction cards.</p><p>As for redirects it would go in turn order, which avoids the loop. So, if you had Decoy Projection and Smoke Bombs in play, in that order, Visionary would redirect to Decoy and then Smoke Bombs would redirect to the highest, which could be Visinoary.</p>",
