      {
        "id": 56614,
        "name": "Belteshazzar",
        "username": "Belteshazzar",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/e274bd/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-03-29T17:05:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hrm… I have a few things that don't sit totally well with me.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"pwatson1974\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/48/1925_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> pwatson1974:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>Determine all damage boosts that apply to the originator in order. Here's where Meteor Swarm stops damage occurring.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>If Meteor Swarm said it prevented damage from being dealt, I would totally agree with this. But Meteor Swarm makes all targets immune to damage, implying that it would be applied immediately before your step 9.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"pwatson1974\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/48/1925_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> pwatson1974:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"5\">\n<li>Determine nemesis bonus</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I understand why you moved the nemesis bonus to after redirects, but would the nemesis bonus logically align with Step 3? e.g. villain decides to damage its nemesis, so damage increases by one along with other originator-side damage changes, and the attack is then redirected. (Though I could see this rationalized either way; this is one reason our group doesn't play with nemesis bonuses… it adds one more thing to keep track of, and we feel like removing it doesn't take away from the game. [Not that I'm saying nobody should use nemesis bonuses; I'm just saying we don't and why.])</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"pwatson1974\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/48/1925_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> pwatson1974:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"7\">\n<li>Check for damage amount based redirects (Driving Mantis, Synaptic Interruption etc). If these apply, go back to the start with the new target.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>So do you reapply, say, obsidian fields after Fixer redirects an attack that's already been reduced to 1 or 2? I was under the impression that redirects do not reapply damage bonuses, but if you go back to the start, do you just skip that step?</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"pwatson1974\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/48/1925_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> pwatson1974:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As for redirects it would go in turn order, which avoids the loop. So, if you had Decoy Projection and Smoke Bombs in play, in that order, Visionary would redirect to Decoy and then Smoke Bombs would redirect to the highest, which could be Visinoary.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Does Decoy Projection use redirect language or \"would take\" language?</p>\n<hr>\n<p>I'm not trying to be a pain about this, but it just seems like strict adherence to play order is worthwhile for some things (start of turn/end of turn) but cumbersome for others (this entire conversation <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> ).</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:31:42.071Z",
